    {
      "id": "accessibility",
      "label": "UI Automation and accessibility acceptance",
      "status": "partial",
      "summary": "Core names and native peers support actionable patterns and virtual-row discovery. Host wrappers skip Tab stops. User reports Narrator/scaling acceptance. Scoped palettes follow contrast settings; TextBox uses frozen normal colors and conditional system resources. ThemeStyles batches resource publication with caller-aware initialization ownership. All 146 framework tests pass, including five accessibility acceptance tests and two resource-ownership checks. Discovery setup initializes native UIA on an MTA client while pumping the window dispatcher, then refreshes cached peers; original assertions pass in the full suite and two additional fresh hosts. Latest seven-pair runtime performance passes 32/32; test-only correction does not change that candidate. Physical contrast acceptance remains open and FW-005 separately awaits IME acceptance. FW-006 is not complete.",
      "sources": [
        "UI Framework/View.cs",
